---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import Grid from '../../components/Grid.astro';
import Card from '../../components/Card.astro';
import { ORG } from '../../consts';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Corporate Sponsorship"
  description="Sponsor the Florida Lantern Project. Verification details, EIN, and sponsorship options for Florida businesses."
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow="For businesses"
    title="Sponsor a program, an event, or a storm response"
    lede="Florida businesses weather the same hurricanes their customers do. Sponsoring the response is a visible way to be part of it."
  />

  <Section title="Everything your giving team needs to verify us">
    <p>
      Most corporate giving programs stop at the verification step. So here it is
      up front, rather than three clicks deep.
    </p>
    <dl class="facts">
      <div><dt>Legal name</dt><dd>{ORG.legalName}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>EIN</dt><dd>{ORG.ein}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Status</dt><dd>501(c)(3) public charity</dd></div>
      <div><dt>State</dt><dd>Florida &middot; registration {ORG.flRegistrationNumber}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Address</dt><dd>{ORG.address.street}, {ORG.address.city}, {ORG.address.region} {ORG.address.postalCode}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Formerly</dt><dd>{ORG.formerName}</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p class="note">
      If your form asks for a determination letter or recent filings, they're on
      the <a href="/about/transparency">transparency page</a>. If it asks for
      something we haven't published, email us and we'll send it the same day.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="surface" title="Ways to sponsor">
    <Grid>
      <Card title="Program sponsorship" meta="Year-round">
        <p>Underwrite a specific service — inspections, readiness kits, or a neighborhood weather station with your name on it.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="Disaster response sponsorship" meta="Activated by event">
        <p>Commit in advance to a named storm response. The money is there the day it's needed, which is the whole difficulty.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="Event sponsorship" meta="Seasonal">
        <p>Our annual Beacons of Hope gala, and the return of the light show as Lanterns of Hope.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="In-kind goods and services" meta="Any size">
        <p>Hotel rooms, transport, supplies, professional services. Our 2024 response ran almost entirely on donated capacity.</p>
      </Card>
    </Grid>
  </Section>

  <Section title="A note on in-kind gifts">
    <p>
      We're grateful for every donated item, and we've learned to be honest about
      what they're worth to us. Goods donated to our 2025 auction carried a stated
      retail value of around $11,700 and realized about $3,300.
    </p>
    <p>
      So if you're choosing between donating a product and sponsoring a program,
      the sponsorship does considerably more — and we'd rather tell you that than
      book the larger-sounding number.
    </p>
    <p><a class="btn" href={`mailto:${ORG.email}?subject=Corporate%20sponsorship`}>Start a conversation</a></p>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .facts { display: grid; gap: 0; margin: var(--space-md) 0; }
  .facts > div {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(9rem, 14rem) 1fr; gap: var(--space-sm);
    padding: 0.7rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  dt { font-weight: 700; }
  dd { margin: 0; }
  .note { font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--color-text-muted); }
  @media (max-width: 520px) { .facts > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.1rem; } }
</style>
